/ActualText (The diagram illustrates the process of producing biofuel named ethanol from start to completion.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Overall, the process entails 8 steps, starting from growing plants and trees for ethanol and culminating in this biofuel being used for different purposes, such as for cars and trucks.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (To begin with, plants and trees are planted where energy from sunlight and carbon dioxide is used before they are harvested. Subsequently, the harvested plants and trees undergo the pre-processing process in order to create cellulose as a by-product.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In terms of the production process of ethanol, after cellulose is processed, sugars are made an outcome. In the following phase, a variety of microbes are added/incorporated into the sugars made from the processing step, which results in ethanol. In the final step, ethanol is utilized for a number of purposes, ranging from cars to airplanes. However, it is interesting to note that these vehicles emit/release CO2, which* will in turn be used as a source for growing plants for ethanol.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
