457 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Whereas the pie chart compares information regarding the locations of dance classes attended by young people in Australia, the bar chart shows the kinds of these classes by different age groups.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
458 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Overall, it can be clearly observed that while the majority attend private studios, ballet is the most popular class among people in the under-11 age group.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
459 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Starting with the locations of these classes, the largest proportion attend private studios, accounting for 48%, although only 10% use college-based studios, which makes up the lowest percentage. It is interesting to note that 24% of young individuals use school halls after school for dancing.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
460 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In terms of the types of classes, ballet is the most popular among children under 11 years old with over 600 enrollments*, whereas modern dance is the least popular in this age group with only 300 students. On the other hand, modern dance has the highest number of participants aged between 11 and 16 years old with over 520 students*; meanwhile, ballet has the lowest number of students in this age range.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
