751 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (To begin with, it might seem reasonable for some to believe that more selections in one supermarket is a positive trend. To explain it simply, this is because it offers more diversity; therefore, consumers can have more selections from all over the world. Take Villa Market in Bangkok, for example; clients have access to food imported from different parts of the world, ranging from apples from China to cheese from France. From this perspective, it is logical why some would argue that this is a positive development for society as a whole.)
/E (To begin with, it might seem reasonable for some to believe that more selections in one supermarket is a positive trend. To explain it simply, this is because it offers more diversity; therefore, consumers can have more selections from all over the world. Take Villa Market in Bangkok, for example; clients have access to food imported from different parts of the world, ranging from apples from China to cheese from France. From this perspective, it is logical why some would argue that this is a positive development for society as a whole.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1 2 3 4]
>>
endobj
752 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (On the other hand, I would personally argue that this is detrimental for communities and individuals. This is due to the fact that it can not only lead to the loss of cultural identity but it can also cause environmental impacts, such as pollutions from the international/ transnational transport of goods. For instance, surveys in 2020 found that 50% of Thai children were not familiarized with traditional Thai food; instead, they preferred international food. In this sense,  it is evident that the availability of international food can be detrimental to cultural uniqueness. )
/E (On the other hand, I would personally argue that this is detrimental for communities and individuals. This is due to the fact that it can not only lead to the loss of cultural identity but it can also cause environmental impacts, such as pollutions from the international/ transnational transport of goods. For instance, surveys in 2020 found that 50% of Thai children were not familiarized with traditional Thai food; instead, they preferred international food. In this sense,  it is evident that the availability of international food can be detrimental to cultural uniqueness. )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5 6 7 8]
>>
endobj
